{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfSHJitxnHowkGuFytjew","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 06 is done. Everything is written and verified, well inside the wall-clock cap.\n\n**What was built**\n- A `fan_order` flag (`\"index\"` default, `\"degree\"` optional) on `decide` in Python and C, and on `restricted_dfs`, registered as `cs-dfs+degree`. One shared definition, `fan_sort_key` in `satisfiability/heuristics.py`: cheapest first, then most neighbours not yet closed, then index. That is §7's two-key rule read as a fan order.\n- The C gained a new entry point and kept `cs_decide` with its old signature, so the recertify run that has been up since Wednesday keeps calling what it always called. The library is now also built to a scratch name and renamed into place. Recertify's nine processes were unchanged before and after.\n- `learning/fan_order.py`: item 01's protocol on 50,896 instances (campaign 10 to 75, corpus 9 to 100), both configurations, both fan orders, both sides of the optimum, plus the DFS bound. 9.25 core-hours, 35 minutes on 16 workers.\n\n**Audit, all clean.** Zero status disagreements between fan orders in 407,168 decision calls, zero contradictions, every witness within the optimum. The default arm reproduces every recorded node count on record (50,756 of 50,756, 30 of them at the six significant digits the upward CSV stored) and every recorded `cs-dfs` value.\n\n**Finding.** The kill criterion is met for both configurations. The refutation's paired median is exactly 1.000 at every size, the p10 to p90 band stays within one percent, and seconds match too. The order touches three refutations in four at 75 customers and the effect cancels. The witness search is different: medians still 1.000, but in aggregate the degree order saves a third of the witness-search nodes at 75, mostly on the ridge cells, with a tail where it costs up to 10×. That side is worth about two percent of a descent. The DFS bound improves marginally and runs slower in Python.\n\n**Proposed, not applied.** Keep `index` for `decide`. Consider `degree` only for satisfiable-side drivers such as the ratchet. Leave `cs-dfs` alone; §7's rule as the seed is the measured route to a stronger bound.\n\n**Records.** Report §20 in `reports/ml_nature.md`, full tables in `reports/fan_order_tables.md`, data in `learning/data/ensemble/fan_order.csv.gz` (2 MB). Ten new tests; full suite 939 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed. PROGRESS.md has the iteration 6 entry with the count at 6 of 14, and item 06 is marked done in `iterations.md`. Eight items remain, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE`. Nothing committed and nothing written to `solutions/`.\n\n**Next for item 07.** The new CSV already holds 50,896 paired post-fix counts under both configurations, so Theorem 2's decision boundary can be fitted from it before any new run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1516,"cache_read_input_tokens":234038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83785eb1-e3da-40dc-ab81-5e292797d013","uuid":"041c8bca-9908-4ff8-8f9f-4c009857582f","timestamp":"2026-09-26T15:24:23.351Z","request_id":"req_011CfSHJiB4VLBrj7sqjZ66t"}
